missing.why:
The draft has no service procedures. Missing:
- how the in-boss guard is serviced (it needs a tray drain);
- who owns the tray cartridge and at what interval;
- PCM rework;
- how an LM 'factory pre-wetted FRU with 5-year inspection' interacts with GPU or package RMA;
- the back-flush procedure;
- spares and MTTR.
Without the tray cartridge, which is only 'recommended' for R-grade, the 25 cm2 guard becomes the loop filter. Scaled from physics/fouling-filtration.md, it reaches 50 % blockage in about 65 days at 1e-4 particles/mL and about 6 days at 1e-3/mL.

missing.how_to_fill:
Write a service concept per SKU:
- procedures, intervals tied to the fouling model, tools and owner (OEM, hyperscaler or us);
- a drip-free disconnect sequence;
- an LM handling SOP and RMA flow;
- guard and cartridge life with and without the tray cartridge, quantified at 1e-4 to 1e-2 /mL.
Decide whether the tray cartridge is mandatory for the R-grade. If it is, drop 'drop-in'.

missing.why:
Leak-before-break is asserted, but the stack has about 6 external perimeter braze seams against 1 on the incumbent (verify-manufacturing). Also missing:
- integration with OCP ACS leak detection (drip trays, rope sensors);
- a leak-rate or FIT target;
- liquid-metal escape: Ga-In is conductive (shorts), and Ga embrittles aluminium, yet close-the-losses proposes Al load frames;
- HV safety for PRISM-DC at 800 VDC on a shared conductive PG25 loop (isolation, creepage, stray-current corrosion).
PRISM's low dP makes negative-pressure (leak-proof) loops feasible at 18 LPM with dual UQD08, a safety differentiator the draft does not use.

missing.how_to_fill:
Add a sustainability section with:
- return temperature against flow and TIM for PRISM and CoolIT;
- ERF and heat-reuse value for a reference 100 MW site in DE and Nordics;
- a WUE model for three climates (adiabatic hours removed by +2-7 K);
- an ISO 14067 cradle-to-gate CO2e per plate against lifetime pump and chiller savings;
- a PFAS-free bill of materials (EPDM, PPSU/PEEK, non-fluorinated dam) with qualification in E5.
